A||||11||Songman||Fiero Voice Chat||||14||
Z||000000||Songman||01-19-2001||07:54 PM||||After talking to Cheever, Sqoach, and a few others in the live chat room the other night, I decided to add a voice chat room to my Fiero site like the one I use on some of my other sites.<P>The Voice Chat Room is up and running now and of course, everyone is invited! There is nothing to sign up for and nothing to download. For some reason though, the room does not work well with Netscape. Internet Explorer 4.0 or better is required.<P>I hope everyone will come by and try it out. Even if you don't have a mic, or if you just don't want to 'talk', there is still a text chat window there too. This could be a really good resource for people that have problems and need to actually 'ask' there question of someone instead of just type it. Meet here and get your answers!<P>Just click on the Tennessee Fiero Owners link in my signature and select Voice Chat.<P>Hope to see you all there!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Songman||01-19-2001||08:14 PM||||Just my luck! I built the voice chat page, tested it, posted a message here about it.. and then when I checked my e-mail there was a message form the software company informing me of a coding change....<P>I'll try to get it up and running in an hour or so....<P>Sorry about the inconvenience...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||01-19-2001||08:19 PM||||Will check into it when I get home.<BR>Got video?  I have one of them cheapo Logitech cameras, but no microphone yet.<BR>Anyway, I'll be watching, er, listening for your progress.<BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||6
Z||000003||2xsess||01-19-2001||09:22 PM||||and we wait  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">   <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||01-19-2001||09:27 PM||||I appreciate your patience, guys...<P>Apaprently the company that I was using for the voice chat server, HearMe, sold out to another company called Telcopoint... and they did this with no warning. Telcopoint is changing all the rules! I was in the room an hour before I posted he message and everything was great! I have looked around the net and every HearMe voice chat room is now dead! And there were thousands!<P>I just hope that Telcopoint runs the chat server software better than they do their website. Nothing works on it and it drags trying to load too. <P>Hopefully, I'll have something up soon...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||01-20-2001||12:10 AM||||You get what you pay for..... I won't use any of the free web servers or any of the free services like above. (I barely tolerate Net Meeting on ocasion. I prefer the defunct PGP phone.)<P>1. they do things like above or they go bankrupt.<P>2. the terms of service on most of the free web servers are discusting.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Songman||01-20-2001||12:40 AM||||I generally agree with you, Ogre, but these guys have been great for months now! I'm really shocked...<P>And I have spent the last three hours trying to find something to replace them with, even something to pay for, and I can't find anything...<P>If anyone has a suggestion, I am open to it...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||9
Z||000007||theogre||01-20-2001||08:15 PM||||net meeting. It's on practically every win9x or NT running.<P>All the Free/Ad based services are taking a pounding. Net Zero recently instituted a 40hr limit per month. Several other "free" ISPs are simply gone.....<P>I'm not supirsed it was shut off with no warning. There have been a number of things sudenly closed recently. It is so bad in some cases employees are simply being locked out of the facility.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Songman||01-20-2001||09:32 PM||||Is there anyway to set up NetMeeting where it is accessible just by clicking on a link on a page?<P>Personally, I deleted it from my system. Not really interested in stuff like that.<P>The good thing about the system I had was that you didn't have to download anything or sign up for anything. Just show up and talk... That was the thing I really liked about it. I want to make my sites so everyone can participate...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||2birds||01-20-2001||10:53 PM||||To quote Neil Peart, "You can't get something for nothing."  <BR>I'm amazed at sites like this one.  Maybe I'm naive, but the Forum rules.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Songman||01-21-2001||01:03 PM||||Thank Cliff for this Forum! Believe me, he didn't get it for nothing. I use this software on two of my sites and it is not cheap!<P>I wasn't using the HearMe software for the chat because it was free. I was using it because it was the coolest chat client I found after searching through lots of options. For the reason I mentioned above (no download, no signup, etc) I just chose it over any other.<P>I wouldn't have minded them giving an option to pay for the service. But they didn't. They just sold the technology to a company that doesn't have their stuff working yet....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Songman||01-21-2001||01:04 PM||||On another note...<P>I do have a chat site up and running. It is pretty nice although a little slow. It is just intended to suffice until Telcopoint gets the voice chat site working...<P>You will have to let a small plugin be loaded before you can join, but after that it is just a java room like any other. Come on by and try it out....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
